owing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ForwardSyntax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ForwardSyntax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ForwardSyntax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ForwardSyntax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ForwardSyntax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ForwardSyntax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ForwardSyntax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ForwardSyntax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-02T23:23:59Z","updated_at":"2026-04-02T23:23:59Z","body":"I have been unable to reproduce this issue since. It's very likely that I just haven't been using Godot for long enough to trigger the bug, as usually I use Godot for around an hour per session, not 2+ unless I lock in. This isn't the issue being done and over with, more, I need more time to reproduce the issue. This comment is more or less just indicating I'm still using Godot to try and reproduce this bug! Thanks for your patience. :D","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4180977989/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4210396232","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117714#issuecomment-4210396232","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117714","id":4210396232,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc769YxI","user":{"login":"ForwardSyntax","id":170281011,"node_id":"U_kgDOCiZIMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/170281011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ForwardSyntax","html_url":"https://github.com/ForwardSyntax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ForwardSyntax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ForwardSyntax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ForwardSyntax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ForwardSyntax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ForwardSyntax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ForwardSyntax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ForwardSyntax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ForwardSyntax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ForwardSyntax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-08T23:30:35Z","updated_at":"2026-04-08T23:33:47Z","body":"Aha! It happened again! After saving the contents of journalctl -b -1 to log.txt, and looking at the very end of the file, i could find \"Apr 08 19:20:46 coollinuxpc kernel: watchdog: BUG: soft lockup - CPU#9 stuck for 27s! [Renderer:907574]\" at the very end of the file. (Though, soft lockup suggests there's a way to unfreeze the computer after this happens? Or maybe it's referring to the fact I can still move my mouse and hear audio, as in the computer is still running, just... not very well.)\nIt may also be worth noting that each of the times my computer has frozen, I've been in the code/script editing interface of Godot, not the 2d or 3d scenes.\nIf you need any more info, please do let me know!!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4210396232/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4222242756","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117714#issuecomm